#Протокол_Step_Parser_Roundtrip<[
Базис:
  Formatter already owns the canonical StepAtomDraft -> .bvc write path.
  Atom Inspector Form, migrations and imports need the reverse path without making raw .bvc editing the normal authoring mode.
  Existing Work Graph parsing is work_item-specific and should not be the generic StepAtomDraft import contract.
Вектор:
  Parser reads canonical atom blocks #Name<[ ... ]> and returns StepAtomDraft-like import records: draft, warnings and errors.
  draft contains profile, name, basis, vector, goal, labels and optional checks/evidence.
  profile is read from labels.atom.profile; missing or unsupported profile is reported through validateStepAtomDraft errors, not silently guessed.
  Базис, Вектор and Цель become ordered arrays of trimmed single-line strings.
  Optional Проверки becomes checks; legacy критерии_готовности is accepted as checks with an import warning.
  Optional Свидетельства becomes evidence as ordered human-readable strings; structured Evidence v1 parsing is later work.
  Метки is the machine envelope; valid key/value rows are preserved as labels without profile-specific projection.
  Legacy top-level machine fields such as guid, id, mode, статус, status and trace_status are read only for import and converted to labels with warnings.
Цель:
  Formatter, parser, form preview and migration code share one stable StepAtomDraft boundary while keeping .bvc human-readable.

Проверки:
  parser returns StepAtomDraft-like records with warnings and validation errors
  format(parse(format(draft))) is stable for canonical formatter output
  Базис, Вектор, Цель, Метки, optional Проверки and Свидетельства are covered
  legacy top-level machine fields import as labels with warnings
  MVP implementation and tests exist in src/stepAtomFormatter.mjs and tests/stepAtomFormatter.test.mjs

Метки:
  atom.profile: prompt_rule
  protocol.id: step-parser-roundtrip
  schema.input: schemas/step-atom-draft.v1.json
  work.source: design-step-parser-roundtrip
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Roundtrip_Invariant<[
Базис:
  The formatter is the canonical serializer for new writes.
Вектор:
  The required invariant is format(parse(format(draft)).draft) === format(draft) for valid StepAtomDraft input.
  Parser may normalize imported legacy text into formatter-compatible arrays, labels and section names, but the second format must be stable.
  The invariant applies to the canonical subset produced by formatStepAtomDraft: Базис, Вектор, Цель, optional Проверки, optional Свидетельства and sorted Метки.
  Parser diagnostics do not change formatter output unless the caller explicitly edits the returned draft.
Цель:
  Atom Inspector can preview an existing atom, reformat it and detect whether a save proposal is a no-op before touching canonical files.

Метки:
  atom.profile: trace
  contract.id: step-parser-roundtrip-invariant
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Preserve_Vs_Normalize<[
Базис:
  Import must preserve meaning while allowing canonical writes to stay deterministic.
Вектор:
  Preserve atom name, section item order, label keys and label values, checks order and evidence order.
  Preserve unknown but syntactically valid labels; profile-specific consumers may warn separately, but the generic parser should not drop them.
  Normalize indentation, surrounding whitespace, optional bullet markers in list sections and label ordering on write through the formatter.
  Normalize legacy критерии_готовности into checks and legacy top-level machine fields into labels, with warnings.
  Do not preserve comments, blank-line layout, duplicate label rows, or legacy top-level machine field placement in the canonical write path.
  Do not infer missing required semantic fields from atom name except as a future profile-specific migration rule; MVP reports validation errors.
Цель:
  Existing .bvc can be imported safely, but formatter-produced output remains the only canonical new-write shape.

Метки:
  atom.profile: architecture_decision
  decision.id: step-parser-preserve-normalize
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Diagnostics_And_Legacy_Warnings<[
Базис:
  LLM and operator tooling need actionable diagnostics rather than hidden repair.
Вектор:
  errors are blocking validateStepAtomDraft messages: invalid/missing profile, invalid atom name, empty required BVC arrays, multiline values or invalid label keys.
  warnings are non-blocking import notes: legacy top-level machine fields, legacy criteria section, ignored malformed label lines and future duplicate semantic aliases.
  Legacy field conversion is read-only compatibility: guid -> labels.guid, id -> labels.atom.id, mode -> labels.atom.mode, статус/status -> labels.work.status and trace_status -> labels.trace.status.
  New writes must not emit legacy top-level machine fields; formatter always writes machine data through Метки.
Цель:
  Import callers can show warnings in the inspector while still allowing a valid draft to be formatted.

Метки:
  atom.profile: prompt_rule
  rule.id: parser-diagnostics-legacy-warnings
  trace.status: verified
]>

#MVP_Implementation_Plan<[
Базис:
  The useful first slice is small because formatter output has a narrow deterministic grammar.
Вектор:
  Implement parseStepAtomDrafts(text) beside formatStepAtomDraft and validateStepAtomDraft.
  Return an array of import records with draft, warnings and errors so callers can parse multi-atom .bvc files.
  Keep WorkGraph parseWorkItems as a work_item projection for now; later it can consume parseStepAtomDrafts after behavior parity tests.
  Cover parser tests for canonical parse, roundtrip stability and legacy field warnings.
  Later add source ranges, block hashes, duplicate label diagnostics, malformed atom recovery and Atom Inspector proposal integration.
Цель:
  MVP unblocks parser roundtrip evidence without expanding into a full .bvc compiler.

Метки:
  atom.profile: trace
  contract.id: parser-mvp-implementation-plan
  trace.status: verified
]>
